 the `sum_field` metric on the declared input and compares the output and its hash with the declared artifacts, rejecting cases such as hidden rubric leakage or an undeclared artifact hash.","claim_id":"claim::research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay","evidence_class":"algorithmic_projection","evidence_strength_rank":3,"organ_id":"research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay","truth_accounting_bucket":"source_faithful_refactor","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay run --input fixtures/first_wave/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay/input --out receipts/first_wave/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"59dcd28ace8ae81785d87e7b223731e8b19065e6ab3af2f8fd113e5477e6321c","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"algorithmic_projection","family":"research_and_science_replays","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"source_faithful_refactor"},"component_id":"research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay","plain":"When a team says it repeated a study's results, a reader needs evidence that the repeat was run and not described. This component reads made-up replay records listing a study's contributions, scoring checklist, output files, scoring script and rerun evidence. It compares the declared fingerprints of the output files, short codes that change when a file changes, with those of the rerun, and adds up the input rows itself to check the one supported score. The output lists findings and rejects a record that cites a file nobody declared or leans on a report with no rerun.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay.md","sha256":"ee93c02bc3a1f103f236d83d5919f676101ce7bee6deec7b2189c4565f697068","text":"# Check a research replication record\n\n> **In plain terms.** When a team says it repeated a study's results, a reader needs evidence that the repeat was run and not described. This component reads made-up replay records listing a study's contributions, scoring checklist, output files, scoring script and rerun evidence. It compares the declared fingerprints of the output files, short codes that change when a file changes, with those of the rerun, and adds up the input rows itself to check the one supported score. The output lists findings and rejects a record that cites a file nobody declared or leans on a report with no rerun.\n\nThis validator reads research replay rows describing contributions, rubric, artifacts, metric scripts and rerun evidence. It checks the declared artifact-hash roster against execution artifacts and reports findings alongside a validation receipt. For the supported public `sum_field` metric specification, it hashes the metric and input bodies, computes a sum over the input rows, and compares the output and its hash with the declared artifacts.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root, with Python 3.11 or newer and the checkout dependencies available:\n\n```sh\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay run \\\n  --input fixtures/first_wave/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay/input \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay \\\n  --acceptance-out .microcosm/component-guides/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay/acceptance.json\n```\n\nInspect `.microcosm/component-guides/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay_result.json` for the result and findings.\n\nThe fixture includes deliberate negative cases. A passing run means the expected failures were detected alongside the checks of the supplied replay, not that an external study was independently reproduced.\n\n## What the result means\n\nA replay citing an undeclared artifact hash or relying on a report without the required artifact replay is rejected. The interpreter handles the supported metric specification, not arbitrary metric scripts. It does not independently reproduce an outside paper or establish a benchmark result.\n\nRelated reading: [ACM Artifact Review and Badging](https://www.acm.org/publications/policies/artifact-review-and-badging-current).\n\n## Verification\n\nWhen `make component-replays` runs this component, the shared [Dafny-verified replay admission](../formal/replay/README.md) checks observed source and input identities, claim-policy identity, and receipt agreement. The example above runs directly and does not invoke that gate. There is no component-specific formal proof of the metric interpreter, and the tests do not establish an outside replication.\n\n## Source\n\n[Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay.py) · [input](../fixtures/first_wave/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay/input) · [tests](../tests/test_research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay.py) · [historical sample result](../receipts/acceptance/first_wave/research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay_fixture_acceptance.json) · [component record](../core/paper_module_capsules.json).\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#RUNTIME_STEPS","src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#_accepted_organ_runner_module_refs"],"declared_prerequisites":{"availability_status":"not_assessed_by_index","description":"Lean, Swift and test extras required","s